While PENDING the dialog showed the 'Preservation is ON…' text above the
pending notice (contradictory) and the positive button read 'Disable
preservation' while nothing was preserved yet. Now the ON text appears
only when STAMPED; PENDING shows the pending notice alone and the button
reads 'Cancel activation' (new English-base string
AliGramPreservationCancelActivation). The toggle action itself is unchanged.

The decision is a pure function (AliGramEligibility
.resolvePreservationDialogState, null state treated as PENDING, opt-out
wins) covered by 5 new JVM tests in AliGramPreservationDialogTest.
